@title INC-3302: Late nightly sales reports
@subtitle Postmortem, Marrow Retail, incident date 2026-10-06
@author Data Platform team, Owner
@date 2026-10-06

kpi Reports late by | 8 h 40 min | due 03:00 UTC, sent 11:40 | bad
kpi Store managers affected | 214 | got empty or stale reports | bad
kpi Backfill duration | 95 min | ran serially | neutral

## Summary

On 2026-10-06 the point-of-sale vendor added a column named `tender_subtype` to the sales feed without notice. The ingestion job failed on it. The failure alert went to a retired channel, so nobody knew until a store manager asked why the report was empty. The reports were due at 03:00 UTC and went out at 11:40.

## Timeline

All times UTC.

table = time,event; 01:15,Vendor deploys the schema change; 02:10,Ingestion job fails for the first time; 02:40,Retries exhausted; 03:00,Reports miss their deadline and no alert fires; 07:25,A store manager asks in #retail-ops why the report is empty; 07:50,Support pages the Data Platform on-call; 08:35,Cause identified; 09:20,Schema mapping patched; 10:05,Backfill starts; 11:40,Reports published

## Contributing factors

- The alert still routed to the retired channel #data-alerts-old.
- There was no schema contract check on vendor feeds.
- The backfill ran serially.

## What went well

- Once paged, the on-call found the cause in 45 minutes.
- No wrong numbers were published.

## Action items

table = action,owner,due; Route pipeline alerts to the on-call pager,Samuel Achterberg,2026-10-16; Add a schema contract check on vendor feeds,Lucia Fontaine,2026-11-06; Parallelize the backfill by partition,Data Platform on-call,2026-11-20; Require 14 days' notice of feed changes in the vendor contract,Vendor Management,2026-10-30
